<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#maloango">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maloango</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ma Loango</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maloango, or Ma Loango, was the title of the king of Loango on the Atlantic coast north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congo-river">Congo River</a>. The holder was a sacred ruler chosen from princes of the royal matrilineage, surrounded by taboos and assisted by officials in charge of trade, war and the coast. The title survived the French colonial conquest as a traditional office.</p></div>
